---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icons from '../components/Icons.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Contact | NutritionColours"
  description="Contact NutritionColours about educational content, corrections, source questions, privacy requests, or general website feedback."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Contact', path: '/contact' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
      <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
        <li><a href="/" class="font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-400 hover:underline">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
        <li aria-current="page" class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-200">Contact</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <div class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-emerald-300 dark:border-emerald-800 bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 px-3.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300">
      <span class="inline-block h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      Editorial Desk & Inquiries
    </div>

    <h1 class="mt-4 text-fluid-hero font-black text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-50 brand-font">
      Questions & inquiries
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 pl-5">
      For editorial corrections, peer-reviewed source submissions, privacy requests, or general website feedback, please contact our administrative desk.
    </p>

    <!-- Channels Grid -->
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="card-interactive rounded-3xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 p-7 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-100">Editorial & Corrections</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
          Spotted an outdated citation, ambiguous phrasing, or want to submit recent trial literature?
        </p>
        <a
          href="mailto:info@nutritioncolours.com?subject=Editorial%20Feedback"
          class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-stone-700 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-stone-800 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 hover:border-emerald-600 transition-colors"
        >
          info@nutritioncolours.com
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="card-interactive rounded-3xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 p-7 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-100">Privacy & Governance</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
          Inquiries regarding data rights under the DPDP Act or website governance standards.
        </p>
        <a
          href="mailto:privacy@nutritioncolours.com?subject=Privacy%20Inquiry"
          class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border border-stone-300 dark:border-stone-700 bg-stone-50 dark:bg-stone-800 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 hover:border-emerald-600 transition-colors"
        >
          privacy@nutritioncolours.com
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Safety Boundary Callout -->
    <section class="mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-amber-300 dark:border-amber-800/60 bg-amber-50/80 dark:bg-amber-950/30 p-6 md:p-8 text-amber-950 dark:text-amber-200 space-y-3" aria-labelledby="safety-notice-heading">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <span class="inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-200/80 dark:bg-amber-900/60 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 border border-amber-300 dark:border-amber-700/80" aria-hidden="true">
          <Icons name="alert-triangle" size={16} />
        </span>
        <h2 id="safety-notice-heading" class="text-lg font-black text-amber-950 dark:text-amber-100">
          Clinical Boundary: Do Not Send Medical Records
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
        This inbox is managed by an administrative and editorial team, not clinical triage physicians. Do not transmit personal health records, diagnostic laboratory panels, government identity numbers, payment details, or urgent acute symptoms.
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-300">
        Emergency Note: NutritionColours does not provide emergency medical services. In an acute medical situation, call your local emergency number or visit the nearest emergency facility immediately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Frequently Asked Questions Accordion -->
    <section class="mt-12 space-y-4" aria-labelledby="contact-faq-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-faq-heading" class="text-2xl font-black text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-100 brand-font">
        Common inquiries
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 p-5 shadow-sm transition-all">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-bold text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-100 flex items-center justify-between">
            <span>How fast does the editorial team process correction requests?</span>
            <span class="ml-4 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">
              <Icons name="chevron-down" size={18} />
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 pt-3 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-stone-800">
            Factual and citation corrections are prioritized immediately. Our editorial team reviews the referenced peer-reviewed paper against our claims ledger within 3 to 5 business days. Substantive updates trigger an entry in our public change log.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 p-5 shadow-sm transition-all">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-bold text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-100 flex items-center justify-between">
            <span>Can I request a personalized meal plan or diagnosis?</span>
            <span class="ml-4 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">
              <Icons name="chevron-down" size={18} />
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 pt-3 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-stone-800">
            No. NutritionColours provides general nutritional education only. Individual therapeutic dietary planning requires a licensed healthcare practitioner with direct clinical examination.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-800 bg-white dark:bg-stone-900 p-5 shadow-sm transition-all">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer font-bold text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-100 flex items-center justify-between">
            <span>Where can I read your complete editorial guidelines?</span>
            <span class="ml-4 text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" aria-hidden="true">
              <Icons name="chevron-down" size={18} />
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 pt-3 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-stone-800">
            Our comprehensive evidence grading hierarchy, conflict of interest disclosures, and AI-assistance boundaries are published in full on our <a href="/legal/editorial-policy" class="font-bold text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-400 underline">editorial policy page</a>.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
